# Slack

Call Slack as the connected user through the Slack MCP server connected to
this session. The session's MCP relay attaches the user's credential on every
call; never ask for or handle credentials yourself.

{{ACTION_AVAILABILITY_SECTION}}

## Usage

Read tools (channels, history, replies, users, search) run freely; posting
and uploading are the writes. Read tools that paginate should be capped with
a result limit to keep your context small.

### List channels

### Read channel messages

Channel messages come newest-first in pages; cap the count.

### Read thread replies

Thread replies are addressed by the parent message's timestamp
(e.g. `1700000000.000100`).

### List workspace users

### Look up one user

### Search messages

Workspace-wide message search (e.g. `deploy failed`).

### Post a message (write)

### Upload a file (write)

Shares a local file into the channel/DM; name the channel, the file, an
optional comment, and an optional thread timestamp to reply in a thread.

## Output

Tool results are JSON. Read tools return the items and whether more existed
past the limit; failures carry Slack's `error` code (e.g.
`not_in_channel`, `missing_scope`) — surface `error` rather than retrying
blindly.

## Notes

- Channels/users are referenced by ID (e.g. `C…`, `U…`); resolve names via
  the channels / users tools first.
- Scopes were chosen by the admin. You cannot widen them; on
  `missing_scope`, tell the user which scope is needed.
